  "judgment": "H4 (multiple factors), ordered H3 > H1 >> H2; H5 rejected. H3 (RF perturbation at model input) is the direct trigger: B_d2<->C residual is class-dependent (median nmse 0.008, range ~5e-5..0.020, corr 0.996), and it is the only leg that separates the clean holdout (24/24 clean NPU) from the RF outcome (merged 55/72 = 76.4%). H1 (generation A<->B) is a secondary, class-specific contributor: aggregate RMS/bw gap is small (0.004 rel RMS, 0.0029 bw99) but the pulse shape differs (spectral flatness ratio ~2500x), and GMSK/OQPSK PAPR/bw and AM-SSB RMS/DC differ (DC delta up to 0.411) \u2014 yet those high-generation-gap classes still classify correctly, while 64QAM/128QAM (small generation gap) collapse deterministically under RF. H2 (digital D2) is negligible (nmse 1.8e-04). The 64QAM/128QAM->256QAM collapse is a model-sensitivity x RF-residual interaction on the highest-order QAM (tightest decision boundary), not a gross domain shift: the parallel original-RadioML audit (task2, 419/480 BF16) shows those classes fail only at 0 dB and scattered, never collapsed. Data sufficient to reject H5 (58 recovered tensors + 72-sample classification + 480-frame original baseline).",
